course: dictionary
lesson: 8664
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word «second» is a good example. «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang» uses second as a unit of time, a tiny slice of a minute.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «The second kind you always tell a trusted adult», second is a number in order, the one after the first. Ask yourself: does a time meaning make sense here? It does not, so the order meaning fits.
explain: Some phrases have their own fixed meaning. «In seconds» means very quickly, and «wait a second» means wait a very short time. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: A second is a very short unit of time, and 60 seconds make one minute.
fact: «Second» also means number 2 in order, after the first, as in «the second day».
fact: «Wait a second» means wait a very short time.
fact: «Seconds» can mean a second helping of food, as in asking for «seconds?»
fact: «Second» can also be a verb: to second an idea is to say you agree with it in a meeting.
exercise: «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer.» What does second mean here? | A person who helps | Another helping of food | *A very short unit of time | Number 2 in order, after the first
exercise: «The second kind you always tell a trusted adult.» Which meaning of second fits? | *Number 2 in order, after the first | Seconds of food | To agree in a meeting | A very short unit of time
exercise: Jayden says, «Hang on a second.» What does he mean? | Go back to the start and begin again | *Wait a very short time | Count to two slowly | Wait for exactly one minute
test: «Some rare birds lay a second egg if the first is taken, so a zoo can hatch two chicks instead of one.» What does second mean here? | The best of all | *Another one, coming after the first | A very short time | Second-hand, used before
test: Mia asks, «Can I have seconds?» at dinner. What is she asking for? | *A second helping of food | Goods sold cheap because they have small faults | A shorter wait before pudding | A tiny piece of time
exam: «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds, so only an adult uses it.» What does «in seconds» suggest? | *Very quickly, in a few short seconds | Very slowly, over several days | One after another, in order | At the same time as the adult
